From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:46:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: return sizeof(gclient_s) from G_GetClientSize

G_GetClientSize() returned the number 12676. The server uses it as the
stride between archived client states, so it has to follow the struct.
It now returns sizeof(gclient_s), with a static_assert that this is
still 12676.

No behaviour change in the 32-bit build.
---
 src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp b/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp
index 78b5dbb9..44a33109 100644
--- a/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp
+++ b/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp
@@ -176,7 +176,8 @@ gclient_s *__cdecl G_GetPlayerState(int32_t clientNum)
 
 int32_t __cdecl G_GetClientSize()
 {
-    return 12676;
+    static_assert(sizeof(gclient_s) == 12676);
+    return sizeof(gclient_s);
 }
 
 void __cdecl G_FreeEntities()
